Interpretation
--------------
The previous 16-position Thinker drain batch created 0.7--0.9 second holes in
Talker code arrival.  One-position drain removes those holes.  The shared FIFO
keeps Talker on CPU0 and Mimi on CPU3 while CPU1/2 execute short jobs from both
dispatchers.  Its only spin lock covers enqueue/dequeue; compute is lock-free.
The steady concurrent cadence is still about 99--128 ms for each 80 ms PCM
frame, so uninterrupted real-time playback is not yet guaranteed.  This
deficit must be fixed in model/kernel throughput and must not be hidden by
delaying the first PCM frame.

The trace above intentionally ran without a playback device to isolate model
cadence.  Physical first-frame ALSA acceptance remains pending a live turn on
the deployed always-listening service.
